xnu: SiliconForest's linuxkpi file descriptors can be sent over a Unix socket

fg_sendable() lists the descriptor types SCM_RIGHTS (and fileports) may carry; DTYPE_SFLFILE
(dma-buf, sync_file and DRM syncobj descriptors made by the DRM kexts, bsd/kern/sf_lfile.c)
was not among them, so a GPU-rendering client could not hand a buffer to a compositor.
The fileglob is shared as for any other type; sf_lfile's close runs once, at the last
reference.

Applied by ../kernel.nix, the kernel the collections of m1-dcp and m1-rust-kext are built
on. /dev/dri device descriptors are vnodes and were sendable already.
UPSTREAM: yes.

--- a/src/Kernel/xnu/bsd/kern/kern_descrip.c
+++ b/src/Kernel/xnu/bsd/kern/kern_descrip.c
@@ -395,6 +395,8 @@
 	case DTYPE_PIPE:
 	case DTYPE_PSXSHM:
 	case DTYPE_NETPOLICY:
+	/* SiliconForest: linuxkpi files (dma-buf, sync_file, drm syncobj); see bsd/kern/sf_lfile.c */
+	case DTYPE_SFLFILE:
 		return (fg->fg_lflags & FG_CONFINED) == 0;
 
 	default:
